    "goal": "Implement Slice S1 of docs/specs/deepen-authority-seams.spec.md (Initiative deepen-authority-seams): delete .pi-extension/runtime-stub.ts so the Pi adapter imports host-neutral runtime modules statically, with Pi behavior unchanged. No Kernel, Assurance or Claude adapter behavior changes.",
    "acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "AC1",
        "assertion": "Per D1 of docs/specs/deepen-authority-seams.spec.md (sources E2, U1): plugins/immune-brain/.pi-extension/runtime-stub.ts no longer exists and nothing imports it; no source file under plugins/immune-brain/.pi-extension loads a runtime module through a dynamic import(); the stub's hand-copied structural types and mirrored constants are gone in favor of the real exports. The package-boundary test asserts this through the import graph or behavior instead of pinning stub source text, and still proves: exactly one registered Pi extension path, one bounded enrollment Tool and no command, TUI-only, the test issuer seam excluded from the shipped extension, and the Pi Enrollment adapter reaching Kernel prepare only through runtime/assurance/enrollment. Negative control: a dynamic runtime import in .pi-extension fails the test. Agreed seam: tests/pi-canary-package-boundary.test.ts.",
